WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest
is a United States senator

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
from New Jersey
and a member of the

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:05.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
Senate Judiciary Committee
Please welcome back to the sho

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.740 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Senator Cory Booker.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, Senator?
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. I'm doing well.
It's been a long stretch.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.345 size:75% position:38%
But it's really good
to be on with you.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks.
-It's been a long stretch.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's a lot
going on for you.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.783 line:92%
You're running for re-election

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:19.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you're helping
in the presidential campaign

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are Senate Judiciary
Committee hearings.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you holding up?
-Look, I'm well.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
What worries me
is about the nation,

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
the state of New Jersey,
and our country,

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.831 size:81% position:41% line:92%
as we are in the midst

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.334 size:78% position:39%
of the fourth-largest
mass-casualty event

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the history
of the United States

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
after the Civil War,
World War II,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.473 line:92%
and the pandemic of 1918.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:43.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's growing.
And to see so many folks

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.879 size:88% position:44%
who are not only facing
these health challenges,

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the resulting
financial challenges,

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.550 line:92%
with 40% of American familie

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have children
and food insecurity

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:56.623 line:92%
and eviction crises and more

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.224 line:92%
So, we are a country that,

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
for lack of a better way
of putting it,

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
is walking through the valle
of the shadow of death.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just been
a frustrating stretch that

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:08.635
instead of the Senate gettin
to work on meeting that crisis

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have been rushing through
a Supreme Court justice

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.207 size:84% position:42%
in a way that has never
before seen in history

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
when there's
an ongoing election.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:19.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
As opposed to really focusin
on the hurt and the pain

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.982
and the challenges that
our fellow Americans are facing.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm wondering if,
behind the scenes,

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:28.655 line:92%
your colleagues across the aisle

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
feel any shame
about the hypocrisy

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
of what they did
to Merrick Garland

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:35.261
and how they're rushing
through this confirmation

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:37.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
with just weeks
before the election.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's been times
in the last four years

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:43.870
that I've definitely seen people
express private outrage

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the behavior
of this president,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.109
how he tramples our norms
and breaks our traditions.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:52.145 size:88% position:44%
Unfortunately, with this
Supreme Court justice,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.180 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I've seen no remorse.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's painful
to have the actual words,

00:01:56.182 --> 00:02:00.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
the exact things that
my colleagues said, months ago

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.755 line:92%
that they would not do this.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.756 line:92%
It is one of those more jarring,

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:07.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
almost whiplashing
times of mine in public life

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you see somebody say
explicitly,

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.164 line:92%
that they will not do this

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if they do,
"Use my words against me,"

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:14.701 line:92%
as one of my colleagues said

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, now,
to see it exactly happening.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is not
just hurting, maybe,

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:22.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
those Democrats who are --
who are against this.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.676 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's actually, you know,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
shredding the fabric
of our country

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
and our culture
and our institutions.

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:30.416
Because one of the great,
important things in a democracy,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
for us to function,
is us to have trust.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trust in our institutions.
Trust in truth.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.090 line:92%
Trust in each other's word

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a time where
we don't live in a country

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:40.860 line:92%
where it's authoritarian rule,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
where one who is strong enough
gets to rule the others.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:48.034
We're a nation that necessitates
grace and compromise

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a willingness
to work together

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.538 line:92%
and to find common ground.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:53.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
And unfortunately,
I think this episode

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
is going to have
lasting damage to our country.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:03:00.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
And obviously, putting a perso
on the Supreme Court

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:03.249 line:92%
for a lifetime appointment

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.786 size:88% position:44%
this is going to be felt
for a generation or two.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:09.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were, of course, referrin
to Senator Lindsey Graham

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the "use my words
against me."

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
His hypocrisy has obviousl
been on display.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:19.566
And yet, we sort of had th
hearings for Judge Barrett that,

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:22.202
even one of your colleagues,
Dianne Feinstein, afterwards

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:25.438
complimented Lindsey Graha
for how the whole thing was run.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:29.209
Do you worry that the Democratic
Party didn't do enough

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
to show how illegitimate
these hearings were

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:37.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how unfair
this whole process has been?

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:40.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I actually think that we did

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.322 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You know, there --

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, a lot of times,
the things that we do

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
don't, understandably,
grab the headlines.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:50.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think that this has been
a time where the chorus of

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:54.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
not only my caucus of fellow
Democratic senators,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:58.371
but the voices of so many
Americans, Republicans --

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
Heck, even two
Republican senators

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:03.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
on their side came and said,
"No, this is not right."

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:06.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I've been grateful
to see people on both side

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.513 line:92%
of the aisle coming forward.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:12.085 size:78% position:39%
Even about a hundred
Notre Dame professors

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:14.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
saying kind things
about the nominee

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:16.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
but just saying
this is not right.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.890 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is wrong.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:21.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at a time where, frankly
we have a president

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:25.398 size:75% position:38%
who is openly saying
he will not support,

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:27.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
necessarily,
a peaceful transfer of power

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, if he loses,
this election is rigged.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:34.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
Telling extremist groups
to "stand back and stand by.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.575 line:92%
It's a time where all of u

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
should be concerned
about the coming election

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:44.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, frankly,
doing everything we can

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:47.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
to affirm our common value
and our common virtues.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not just voting.
To me, that is a grave urgency

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:53.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this is going to take
a time, I think, in our countr

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:54.193 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
where many of us

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:58.097
are going to have to step up
in the spirit of civic grace

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:01.000
in a spirit of, you know,
trying to make this nation

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
more of a beloved community,
to help get us through

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
what I think
is going to be a tough period.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.376 line:92%
-You had to ask the nomine

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether or not
she condemns white supremacy

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:15.114
whether or not she support
a peaceful transfer of power

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:18.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you satisfied
with her answers?

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I -- I was --
I was stunned, actually,

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:22.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there was a lot of things
she just refused to answer

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.557 line:92%
things that, I can only imagine,

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:27.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
that in the years
preceding this,

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:30.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
that every appointed judge
or nominated judge

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.165 line:92%
on both sides of the aisle

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:33.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
would find the questions
almost ridiculous.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Do I support
a peaceful transfer of power

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.604 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Of course, I do.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:42.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do I think that climate change
is real?"

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:44.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
That -- I mean,
a lot of the questions,

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:47.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
she just refused
to even express her --

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:50.216 line:92%
her -- her affirmation of.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was a little bit
disturbing to me.

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:54.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when it comes
to issues of race,

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:57.990 size:81% position:41%
which is another issue
I explored with her,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.992 line:92%
I was actually sort of surprised

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:04.430
that someone of
renowned scholarship and writing

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
could not express to me,
really, any kind of critical

00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
or even curiosity to read,
a lot of the literature

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:15.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's out there
about how our legal system

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:18.177 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is so affected by race.

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:20.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
And why --
how we still are a nation

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:23.649
that has a justice system that
has disparate impact on people

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
based upon the color
of their skin

00:06:25.785 --> 00:06:26.819 line:92%
or the wealth that they have

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:29.055 size:81% position:41%
As one of my heroes,
Brian Stevenson, says,

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have a criminal
justice system

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:32.692
that treats you better
if you're rich and guilty

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
than if you're poor
and innocent.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:38.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so to not even being abl
to speak to that

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.132 line:92%
makes me worry about how,

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:43.569
when you are asked to presid
over cases that I think demand

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
first and foremost,
from a judge,

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.240 line:92%
the ability to show true empathy

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:50.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
and understanding
of both sides of an issue,

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:51.711 line:92%
but yet you haven't examined

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:54.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
with any depth, scholarship,
or deep curiosity,

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:57.517 size:88% position:44%
it makes me really worry
about you, in any way,

00:06:57.517 --> 00:06:59.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
being able to make
our justice system

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:03.189
more equal, more accessible,
and more legitimate in the eye

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:05.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the diversity
that is America.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:08.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk more
about race and diversity

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:11.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the ways in which the
President brings your name up.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:15.334
And we'll be right back with
more from Senator Cory Booker.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Right after this.

